    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104642" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρᾱχύ-στομος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of rough speech</i> or
				<i>pronunciation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				14.2.28
			</span></i>, where he couples it with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παχύστομος,</span> and in the same paragraph he writes <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παχυστομέω </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τραχυστομέω</span> cod. E, and so it is cited in <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				367.29
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παχυστομία.</span></div>
